ll\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F01 and F03 print count_noun from a list whose only members are the singular forms centimeter (cm) and meter (m), while answer ranges over 1 to 29 and includes many values other than 1, so a plural number takes a singular noun (for example, a total of 12 printed as 12 centimeter (cm)). F02 draws longer_val from 10 to 50 and shorter_val from 10 to 45 with no ordering stated, so the template can state that dest_a is 10 m from the gate and dest_b is 45 m, then ask how many meters farther dest_a is, which is false. F09 draws longer_val and shorter_val from one unordered list, so the question can ask how much longer the object named as shorter is. F09 also draws longer_obj and shorter_obj from the full object pool with no link to v and v2, so the question can name objects the statement never measured. F06 draws a and b from 10 to 39, so a + b is at most 78 and at least 20, yet the observed answer runs for F06 include 18 and 86 to 87, so the equation can print a false sum. F04, F05, F07, F08 and F10 were checked and their printed values stay within what their templates can state correctly.\"}",
